:: A4_start
<<set $act to 4>><<spend 6>>
<blockquote>Stairs go down into the dark. The air is cold and tastes like old coins. Bones lie in the walls, neat as books on a shelf. Your candle makes the skulls smile.</blockquote>

Behind you, on the stairs: jingle, jingle.

A Silent One is coming down.

There is a gap in the wall, between the bones. Just big enough for you.

[[Squeeze into the gap|A4_hide]]

:: A4_hide
<<spend 1>>
You press your back into the bones. You cover your candle with your hand.

Grey robes pass the gap. A mask with no mouth.

Do not move. Type //wait//.

<<textbox "_guess" "">>
<<link "Do it">><<check _guess "wait|stay|z" "A4_hide_2" "A4_caught">><</link>>

:: A4_hide_2
<<spend 1>>
The keys stop. Right next to you.

You can smell it. Wet wool and smoke.

Type //wait//.

<<textbox "_guess" "">>
<<link "Do it">><<check _guess "wait|stay|z" "A4_hide_3" "A4_caught">><</link>>

:: A4_hide_3
<<spend 1>>
The mask turns. Slowly. It looks into the gap.

It looks right at you.

<div class="heartbeat">Thump. Thump. Thump.</div>

Your heart is so loud.

Type //wait//.

<<textbox "_guess" "">>
<<link "Do it">><<check _guess "wait|stay|z" "A4_hide_done" "A4_caught">><</link>>

:: A4_caught
<<spend 6>>
You move. Only a little. But it is enough.

A grey hand shoots into the gap. You bite it, hard.

You run. Bones fall behind you. Your candle burns fast as you run.

At last the keys are far away.

[[Catch your breath|A4_bridge]]

:: A4_hide_done
<<spend 1>>
The mask turns away. The keys go down the tunnel. Then they are gone.

You breathe again.

The bones make two ways forward.

[[Follow the bones|A4_long]]
<<if $satchel.includes("tunnel_map")>>[[Use your chalk map|A4_bridge]]<</if>>

:: A4_long
<<spend 4>>
The tunnel goes on and on. Left. Right. Down again.

Your candle gets shorter. At last you see water ahead.

[[Go to the water|A4_bridge]]

:: A4_bridge
<<spend 1>>
Black water. Over it, a line of flat stones. Each stone has a name and a short story.

Words on the wall: //Step only on those who loved.//

The first three stones:

* ''Giovanni.'' He kept all his gold. He died alone with it.
* ''Maria.'' She gave her bread to a sick child. She died hungry in winter.
* ''Pietro.'' A great general. He won forty battles.

[[Step on Giovanni|A4_fall]]
[[Step on Maria|A4_bridge_2]]
[[Step on Pietro|A4_fall]]

:: A4_bridge_2
<<spend 1>>
The stone holds. Three more stones:

* ''Beatrice.'' The most beautiful woman in Florence. Many men loved her.
* ''Luca.'' He carried his old father on his back for ten years.
* ''Antonio.'' He built the biggest house on the river.

Luca. Like you.

[[Step on Beatrice|A4_fall]]
[[Step on Luca|A4_drawing]]
[[Step on Antonio|A4_fall]]

:: A4_fall
<<spend 4>>
The stone sinks. Ice-cold water up to your knees.

Your candle almost dies. You hold it high and climb back.

Think. Who loved someone? Not who //was// loved.

[[Try again|A4_bridge]]

:: A4_drawing
<<spend 1>>
On the far side, there is a drawing on the wall. Leonardo's hand. You know it.

It is a map of the church. One piece is missing: the top of the tower.

<<clue "churchmap">>
Under it, in mirror writing:

<div class="mirror">SLAEVER EMIT</div>

Write it the right way round.

<<textbox "_guess" "">>
<<link "Read it">><<mirror _guess "timereveals|time reveals" "A4_drawing_ok" "A4_drawing_wrong">><</link>>

:: A4_drawing_wrong
<<spend 3>>
Read each word from the right. Then put them in order.

[[Try again|A4_drawing]]
[[Give up and go on|A4_rook]]

:: A4_drawing_ok
A stone in the drawing moves. Behind it, words glow:

<<speak "time">>

[[Go on|A4_rook]]

:: A4_rook
A face jumps out of the dark. You almost scream.

It is Rook, grinning.

"Five Silent Ones, behind you. I can lead them away. I know these tunnels."

He points at your satchel. "But I want the old man's mirror. It is worth a lot of money."

<<if $satchel.includes("mirror")>>[[Give him the mirror|A4_give]]<</if>>
[[Say no|A4_refuse]]

:: A4_give
<<take "mirror">><<trust "rook" 2>><<set $flags.gave_mirror to true>>
Rook takes the mirror. For a second, he looks surprised.

"You trust me? Nobody trusts me."

He runs back into the dark, shouting and laughing. The keys follow him.

You are alone. And safe. For now.

[[Go on|A4_end]]

:: A4_refuse
<<spend 6>><<trust "rook" -1>>
"Your loss," says Rook. He is gone.

The keys come closer. You run. You run until your legs burn.

[[Go on|A4_end]]

:: A4_end [autosave]
A deep sound. The ceiling shakes.

Behind you, the tunnel falls in. Stone and dust and bones.

You can only go forward.

And somewhere ahead, something is singing.

[[Go toward the song|A5_start]]
